@page "/guides/dino-level"

@*
    The one page in the app that is behind a real paywall, and the only caller of
    PremiumLock's hard gate. Everything inside that gate is withheld — not blurred — from
    anyone who is not on the perpetual licence, so the method itself must stay inside it:
    the header above the gate says what the page is about and nothing about how it is done.
*@

<header class="page-header">
    <h1 class="page-title">Higher dino levels</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle">How to push a tamed creature's level higher — written down from the owner's own testing</p>
</header>

<PremiumLock RequiresLifetime="true">

    <div class="dlg-layout">

        <section class="content-card dlg-intro">
            <h2 class="dlg-card-title">What this does</h2>
            <p>
                A creature you have already tamed can be freed and tamed a second time. Each pass
                lands at a higher tame level than the one before, so the same creature ends up
                further above where it started without being bred.
            </p>
            <p>
                This is a game mechanic, not a tool in Razor Reaper — there is nothing here to
                click. It is written down from the owner's own testing and worked at the time it
                was written. There is no video for it yet.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="content-card dlg-steps-card">
            <h2 class="dlg-card-title">Step by step</h2>
            <ol class="dlg-steps">
                <li>
                    <span class="dlg-step-head">Unclaim the tamed dino</span>
                    <span class="dlg-step-detail">It has to be unclaimed before anything else works.</span>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="dlg-step-head">Catch it with a Noglin</span>
                    <span class="dlg-step-detail">Take the creature over so the Noglin is holding it.</span>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="dlg-step-head">Upload the Noglin at a transmitter</span>
                    <span class="dlg-step-detail">Put the Noglin itself into the upload, not the creature.</span>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="dlg-step-head">Leave render distance</span>
                    <span class="dlg-step-detail">Move far enough away that the area unloads for you.</span>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="dlg-step-head">Wait until the Noglin is gone from render</span>
                    <span class="dlg-step-detail">Give it time — this is the part that is easy to cut short.</span>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="dlg-step-head">Come back</span>
                    <span class="dlg-step-detail">The creature should be standing there free again.</span>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="dlg-step-head">Tame it again</span>
                    <span class="dlg-step-detail">A normal tame, on the creature you just freed.</span>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="dlg-step-head">Repeat</span>
                    <span class="dlg-step-detail">Every round starts from a higher tame level than the last.</span>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </section>

        <div class="dlg-boxes">

            <section class="content-card dlg-box">
                <h2 class="dlg-card-title">Requirements</h2>
                <ul class="dlg-list">
                    <li>A Noglin — a high level one is likely to be needed.</li>
                    <li>A transmitter to upload the Noglin at.</li>
                    <li>The dino unclaimed before you start.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="content-card dlg-box">
                <h2 class="dlg-card-title">Tips &amp; caveats</h2>
                <ul class="dlg-list">
                    <li>Leave render properly — half out is not out, and the step will not fire.</li>
                    <li>Keep the Noglin safe; you need it again for the next round.</li>
                    <li>Results can differ by server settings, so treat the levels you get as your server's, not a fixed number.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

        </div>

        <p class="dlg-footer">
            Something changed? Tell us via <a href="/feedback">Feedback &amp; Support</a>.
        </p>

    </div>

</PremiumLock>
